WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.138
Physics decides the architecture
because part of every delay on a

2
00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:08.375
wide-area path is simply the time
light takes to travel through glass.

3
00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:13.475
Roughly, it's one millisecond for every
two hundred kilometers of fiber, one way.

4
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:16.663
New York to London has a
round-trip floor of fifty-six

5
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:19.925
milliseconds before any
equipment touches a packet.

6
00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:24.412
Optimization works on the gap above
that floor, never on the floor itself.

7
00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:26.201
There's a common misreading too.

8
00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:30.125
The often-quoted 150-millisecond
voice budget is mouth to ear,

9
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:33.050
and the phones themselves
use a big share of it.

10
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.319
So a West Coast office hairpinning
through northern Virginia

11
00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:39.462
can spend most of the network's
allowance on the detour alone.

12
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:43.962
And a synchronous commit pays a round
trip every time, whatever the bandwidth.

13
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:48.862
The answer is needing less global
synchronization, not faster synchronization.

14
00:00:48.862 --> 00:00:50.900
Which leads to a key distinction.
